{"type": "thinking", "text": "Reverse works for size: Notes, Shopping, Regex2, Money, Indent, todo, Indent2, Regex, Single. It seems consistent reverse of previous order. Good.\n\nNow let's test Name sort (with folder first) reverse? Actually initial name order Indent2, Indent, Money, Notes, Regex2, Regex, Shopping, Single, todo. Reverse should flip. But wait, need to check folder Zeta position with \"folder first\" checked and reverse order. When reverse, folder Zeta stayed first (it's first in reverse list too) because folder first means folders always first. Hmm, that's fine-ish.\n\nBut there might be a bug: quick-access marking. \"File browser quick-access marking: the browser's marks are now kept up to date by its own handlers alone.\" This might refer to long-press context menu option \"Pin to quick access\"? Or the colored marks? Hmm. Let me explore more options.\n\nActually let me focus. Test the sort name ordering more carefully. What about default name sort correctness: Zeta folder, then files. Compare \"Indent2\" vs \"Indent\": depending collation. Let me check with Name sort and reverse.\n\nActually let me test \"Folder local\" option: that's probably \"show local folder\" or something. Hmm, \"Folder local\" could be checkbox \"Show folder in local\"? Not sure.\n\nLet's test sort persistence: go out and back. Sort is set to size desc. Enter Zeta and go back, see if sort persists.\n\nActually let me now test view mode with GFM tables. I need to create a table in a file. The preconditions don't include a table. I can create content in a file via editor (but shouldn't change data outside testing requires — creating a test file is fine? The instructions say do not change data outside what testing requires. Testing tables requires a table). I could edit Notes.md then revert. Better: create a new file for testing? But then file browser changes. Alternatively use Shopping.md and revert. Let's think later.\n\nFirst test file browser quick-access marking. What is