{"type": "thinking", "text": "Saved content = \"kid\". Autosave works. So Save disabled after redo makes sense? Actually back autosaved? No—autosave happened on back at 1:04 with kid content. But at the moment after redo, save was disabled while disk still had \"child\"... Hmm. Unless the \"save\" happened when undo was pressed? Let's reconstruct:\n\n1. Opened Indent.md: content \"child\" from disk.\n2. Search replace child->kid. Editor kid, Save enabled, Undo enabled.\n3. Close search. Editor kid, Save enabled.\n4. Tap Undo. Editor child, Undo disabled, Redo enabled, Save enabled.\n5. Tap Redo. Editor kid, Redo disabled, Save disabled?? That seems wrong because disk content is child.\n\nBut eventually back autosave to kid. So maybe after undo step 4, save enabled, and maybe undo itself triggered a save? No. Hmm, maybe the Save button state being disabled after redo is a real bug in the \"change tracker\" attached once document has content. This is the changed area! \"Editor step back/forward controls: the change tracker is now attached once the document has content.\" Perhaps the bug is that undo/redo state is wrong when document is initially empty. Let's test more carefully with a fresh editor and string typing.\n\nActually let me test the step back/forward when typing normally: open a file, type something, undo/redo. This may reveal bug for \"Single.md\" (content one line no newline) or empty file. Hmm, \"attached once the document has content\" means for empty documents, undo history might not work until content added. Let's test with an empty new file? We shouldn't create files unnecessarily; but testing requires. We could create a temp file then delete it. Or use Single.md carefully and revert.\n\nWait. Let me reconsider the save-state anomaly. It might be simply that autosave occurs when editor loses focus: tapping Undo/Redo toolbar causes focus change and autosave, then the change tracker rebaselines. Actually tapping toolbar might blur editor => autosave triggers? Markor autosaves on pause. Tapping a toolbar button shouldn't pause.\n\nHmm, but the modified time updated only after pressing BACK. So autosave on back. At step 5, disk content likely \"child\"? No wait: after step 4 undo -> child. Disk child. Step 5 redo -> kid. Save disabled = bug (should be enabled since kid not persisted). Then press BACK autosaved kid anyway. So user wouldn't lose data; just button state. Hmm, the \"Save\" button disabled could still be a notable bug: after redo, save disabled but content differs from disk. But does it matter? Since autosave handles it. Lower severity.\n\nLet me instead test undo/redo more systematically with typing. First restore Indent.md to original content. Use search/replace kid->child and save. Let's do that now: search, replace, replace all, close search, back to trigger save. Actually simpler: select all and retype? Use editor, tap in editor, Ctrl+A? No select all button. Use search/replace kid -> child."}
