{"type": "thinking", "text": "Oops! Editor content became just \"x\" — my tap at (540,600) apparently selected all? Or tapping a location where text was and typed replaced everything? Hmm, likely the tap at y=600 hit the editor and cursor placed at end? But content shows \"x\" only, meaning all text got selected (maybe tap when text not focused selects all? Markor's editor might select all on first tap? Hmm). That destroyed the table.\n\nWait, more likely: my tap at (540,600) landed on the editor, placing cursor, but the editor was showing a selection from previous type_text? Actually type_text may select all before typing? No.\n\nRegardless, now content is \"x\". Undo still disabled. Save still disabled even though content changed from saved empty to \"x\"?! Now this is a strong bug: after editing a new file, Save is disabled and Undo disabled. This matches changed area #4. Let me verify by pressing back and reopening: if content persisted as \"x\", autosave works; but the undo control being disabled is definitely wrong.\n\nWait, maybe the buttons' disabled state is just wrong in accessibility because they're `Button` views whose enabled state isn't updated? But we saw in Indent.md Undo became enabled after replace. So it can update.\n\nHmm, difference: Indent.md had content when opened; QATable.md was empty when opened. So for empty documents, the change tracker never attaches -> undo/redo stay disabled forever, and Save maybe remains disabled (though autosave on back may still persist). The hint says \"change tracker is now attached once the document has content\" — meaning they intended to attach when content exists. Perhaps the bug: it's attached only once at content load; for document that starts empty, it never attaches. Hmm, but hint says \"now attached once the document has content\", which sounds like intended fix. The seeded bug might be that the tracker is attached even when document is empty (i.e., attached at start regardless), causing issues? Or attached too early so undo state wrong for loaded files? Hmm.\n\nLet's test scenario with document that starts empty (new file): type text -> undo disabled. Test scenario with document that starts with content (Indent.md): replace -> undo enabled. So bug affects empty documents. That's plausible seeded bug: \"change tracker is now attached once the document has content\" but implementation attaches when document content loaded; for new empty file content empty, tracker not attached, so no undo.\n\nBut wait, maybe undo in Markor only tracks changes after initial load, and for new file first change should be undoable to empty. Undo disabled is wrong.\n\nLet's also test Save for empty-start doc: Save disabled while content \"x\". If Save disabled, maybe the file won't be saved—data loss! Let's press back and check whether content persisted. If not saved, that's severe. Press BACK."}
