{"type": "thinking", "text": "Content persisted as \"hello\". So autosave on back works. The save button disabled isn't data loss. So the real bug is Undo/Redo disabled after edits to a document that was empty when opened. Hmm, but note earlier \"x\" seemed lost upon reopening—it showed empty. Wait, after \"x\" typed, we pressed BACK (keyboard hide), then BACK (leave). Browser timestamp 1:05. Reopen showed empty. Then typed \"hello\", back twice, timestamp 1:06, reopen shows hello. So the \"x\" was lost but \"hello\" persisted? Odd inconsistency.\n\nMaybe the first time, \"x\" replaced all content while keyboard was open, but the autosave didn't occur because... hmm. Actually the first time, file was created in the same session via FAB dialog and maybe not yet \"saved\" until leaving? Hmm, but it showed file with 1:05 timestamp after back. Then reopened empty. So creation wrote empty file, then typing x didn't mark dirty, and no autosave (since not dirty). Wait but the second time hello persisted, meaning dirty marked. Difference: the second time we typed \"hello\" into the editor which was empty and had just been re-opened; maybe the change tracker attached on first text change? But undo/save stayed disabled in observed state. Then back autosaved (maybe because file open session always saves content on close), so hello persisted. For the first x: why didn't it persist? Maybe because the file was newly created and the editor wasn't properly attached to file, so on back it saved empty? Hmm.\n\nActually wait: after creating the file via the new-file dialog, editor showed empty. Typed table; then tapped editor at (540,600), typed \"x\" replacing all content with \"x\" (why? tap may have triggered \"select all\"?). Hmm, maybe the tap at (540,600) hit the editor's long-press selection? No.\n\nThen press BACK once (hide keyboard) — editor \"x\". Press BACK second — left. Browser QATable.md 1:05. Reopened → empty. So content \"x\" lost. But then typed \"hello\" → back back → 1:06 → reopened → \"hello\". Difference? Possibly the first back-after-keyboard-hide triggered autosave of empty? no.\n\nHmm, maybe the first reopen showing empty is because the editor's text hadn't been committed... Actually QATable.md content on disk might have been empty because the file was created as empty and the typed \"x\" session ended without save, and the second \"hello\" session saved because... hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the difference: after first session, pressing back from editor didn't leave because there was no focus? Let me look at the sequence: After typing table, I pressed BACK once → keyboard hidden (still editor). Then tapped at (540,600) to position cursor, keyboard opened. Then typed \"x\" (content became \"x\"). Then pressed BACK → keyboard hidden. Pressed BACK again → browser. QATable.md listed 1:05. Reopened → empty. So lost.\n\nSecond: typed hello in editor (opened empty), Undo/Save disabled. Pressed BACK → keyboard hidden. BACK → browser, QATable 1:06. Reopen → hello persisted.\n\nHmm! Maybe the difference is the file was being edited in the same \"open\" session for the first time right after creation; the file's editor was started with \"new file\" and on exit saved empty because dirty false. Second time, entering editor of an existing empty file attaches differently? This is getting deep. The core user-visible bug: Undo button disabled after typing (both sessions). Save disabled also. That's clearly contrary to expected.\n\nBut for view mode table test, I need content. Currently QATable.md has \"hello\". Let me set the table content. To avoid the tap-select-all issue, I'll select all via long press? Simpler: use search/replace to replace hello with table? Search dialog's search field can input multiline? New Line button exists. But replace field multiline maybe via New Line? Hmm.\n\nAlternative: Tap at end of \"hello\" (tap near x=600,y=299) then press Enter etc. Actually simplest: tap at the end of the line to place cursor after \"hello\", then type text. Tap coordinates: text starts ~180? Actually editor text \"hello\" at top-left. Tap x=540 y=299 might place cursor at end (line is short). Then type \"\\n| Head A |...\"? But the tap earlier replaced content weirdly. Maybe what happened: tapping at (540,600) in empty area below text placed cursor there, but then typing \"x\" replaced all because editor had select-all from type_text? Unclear.\n\nLet me try: tap editor near end of \"hello\" line. Observe keyboard. Then type \"\\n\" + table. Actually I can just clear editor content by selecting all with long-press then \"Select all\" menu? Let's instead use search/replace: search \"hello\", replace with a table string via New Line button? The replace field may allow newline insert with the \"New Line\" button next to search field maybe applies to both. Let's try the search dialog replacement; but typing multiline with type_text might work if I include \\n in text (ADB input text doesn't support \\n; tool may handle? For the table type earlier, \\n worked and inserted newlines! It inserted the full table with newlines. Good.)\n\nSo: search \"hello\", replace with table text, Replace all. Then verify editor content. Then view mode.\n\nLet's do that. Tap search (element 5)."}
