Select All, Undo/Save became enabled. So for the same document (QATable.md) that started empty this session, later edits enabled Undo. Hmm wait—the session that started empty was the \"hello\" open. We then searched and replaced hello->table. Undo/Save stayed disabled while search bar open, but after closing search they became enabled. Hmm, that suggests the tracker updated when the search bar closed and editor regained focus. So maybe no bug at all, just stale UI while keyboard was open? Hmm! Important.\n\nLet's re-examine: After typing \"hello\" initially (empty doc), we observed Undo disabled & Save disabled with keyboard hidden too (after first BACK). Hmm, at that point Undo/Save disabled. So that's not just search bar. But the second session: after replace all via search, closing search made Undo/Save enabled. So the tracker did attach at some point.\n\nMaybe the change tracker attaches when the document has content and a text change occurs, but the toolbar's enabled state update is delayed until some event. In first session, typing \"hello\" then BACK (keyboard) then observe: Undo/Save disabled. Maybe waiting a bit? We didn't wait. Could be UI refresh delay. Second session after closing search: enabled. Hmm.\n\nLet me directly test fresh: QATable currently has table content and view mode. Tap Edit, then select all and type \"abc\" (simple), then hide keyboard, wait, observe undo state. If Undo becomes enabled, then the earlier disabled state was transient because we observed too soon. Let's do this carefully.\n\nActually, more robust test: use an existing precondition file with content (e.g., Single.md one line, no trailing newline) and type a character at end. Verify Undo enabled. Also test the change tracker for \"Single.md\" no trailing newline. That's a boundary case likely relevant.\n\nBut first, the table area. Let's do more table variants. I'll edit QATable again. Tap Edit Mode."}
