{"type": "thinking", "text": "Second undo restored the table. So the first undo removed \"abc\" → empty? Wait the history: selection replace might be two changes: delete selection (all → empty) then insert \"abc\". Actually when typing replaces selection, the text watcher may record deletion and insertion separately. First undo removed \"abc\" (leaving empty), second undo restored deleted table. Hmm, that's arguably acceptable (undo steps through edits), though not ideal. Not necessarily a bug seeded.\n\nBut note \"Editor step back/forward controls: the change tracker is now attached once the document has content.\" Maybe the seeded bug relates to this: when document is emptied completely, the change tracker detaches, so undo stops? Let's test: after first undo (editor empty), Undo was still enabled, so tracker not detached? Hmm.\n\nLet's test the empty-doc scenario again cleanly with a NEW file, since that seems where bug is. But first restore QATable? It currently has table content but after undo 2x, the document equals saved? The saved content may still be table (autosave from before). Fine. Actually we need to delete QATable at the end, since it's test data unrelated to preconditions. We can delete via long press -> Delete. Do that later.\n\nNow let's test the empty doc case with a new file. Create \"QAEmpty.md\". Then don't type immediately? Test:\n1. Create file; editor opens empty.\n2. Type \"test\".\n3. Hide keyboard, wait.\n4. Check Undo/Save states.\n5. Tap Undo (if enabled) or note disabled.\n6. Back, reopen, check content.\n\nBut wait—maybe the earlier problem was caused by not waiting for toolbar update. Actually after typing \"hello\" (empty doc), we hid keyboard and observed immediately: Undo/Save disabled. We didn't wait. Could be delayed. But after typing table via replace in same file, and hiding keyboard (BACK), toolbar still disabled until we closed search (which disabled? no). Hmm: timeline for hello session: type \"hello\" → hide keyboard (BACK) → observed Undo/Save disabled → pressed BACK again → browser. So we did not wait. Maybe wait would fix.\n\nLet's do the new file test with waits to be sure. Create QAEmpty.md via FAB. Need to get to browser. Press BACK twice (we're in editor)."}
