{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now Undo & Save enabled. So the toolbar enable state updates only after the keyboard closes? Wait, in the QAEmpty first session (newly created file), after keyboard close and 3s wait, Undo/Save remained disabled. Second session (reopened file), after keyboard close, Undo enabled. So the bug is specifically: document created fresh (empty at open) → change tracker not attached, so undo doesn't work until... perhaps it attaches when editor reopened with content. This matches \"change tracker is now attached once the document has content\": on open of new empty file, no content ⇒ tracker not attached; but after typing content, tracker should attach — seems it doesn't during that session. Hmm, but in second session, file had content \"test\" at open, so tracker attached, and editing \"X\" → undo enabled.\n\nWait, but after typing \"test\" in first session, content existed, yet tracker not attached. So \"attach once document has content\" isn't triggered by typing, only by loading content at open. That's the bug. Let me verify Undo works after first session's typing? It was disabled, so no.\n\nSo the bug is reproducible: create new empty file, type text → Undo/Redo/Save stay disabled (but autosave on exit). Hmm—but does that matter? Undo doesn't work; that's a real functional bug. Also Save disabled while content unsaved (but autosave on exit). Is there a risk: if app is killed, changes lost? Autosave on pause maybe. Hmm.\n\nWait, but maybe the intended fix \"change tracker is now attached once the document has content\" means it's attached when content arrives (which is what we'd expect) — and maybe the bug is that after the document loses content (select all delete), tracker detaches and undo breaks? Let's test that: In QAEmpty session, select all and delete → doc empty → type → undo? Hmm.\n\nHonestly, the exact seeded bug might be: \"Editor step back/forward controls: the change tracker is now attached once the document has content.\" I interpret: previously the tracker attached in onCreate before content loaded, causing undo to include the initial load as a change (undo would empty the doc). The fix attaches after content loaded, i.e., once. The bug could be that for an empty document, content never loads (empty), so the tracker attaches and then... hmm.\n\nAlternatively, the bug might be that undo resets the whole doc to empty on first undo, as we observed earlier (undo after select-all replaced \"abc\" showed empty first, then table after second undo). Actually that's expected if delete+insert split into two undo steps.\n\nLet's approach differently: maybe there is a seeded bug where Undo becomes enabled but acts wrongly (e.g., undoes too much) for documents loaded with content. Test: open Indent.md, type a char at end, undo once → should remove char only. Earlier we did replace and undo (worked). Let's test typing undo in Single.md (no trailing newline) — boundary input.\n\nBut maybe more productive: check the other changed areas: quick-access marking and search/replace option checkboxes. The \"search and replace dialog: option checkboxes are now placed above the search and replace input fields\" — wait, in the editor search bar, the options are icon buttons. But there might be ANOTHER search/replace dialog: In file browser, \"Search\" dialog has checkboxes below the search field. That's \"option checkboxes\" but no replace. Hmm.\n\nMaybe there's a \"search & replace\" dialog in the editor via \"More options\" -> \"Search & Replace\"? Let's check the editor \"More options\" menu. It likely has actions including \"Search & Replace\". The inline search bar is one thing; maybe the actual \"Search and Replace dialog\" is a separate dialog with checkboxes (regex, case) above two input fields. Let me check \"More options\" in editor.\n\nWe're in QAEmpty editor with content \"X\". Open More options (element 6)."}
