{"type": "thinking", "text": "Tools only Speed Read. No search/replace dialog there.\n\nSo the inline search bar is \"search and replace\". The changed note about \"option checkboxes are now placed above the search and replace input fields\" might refer to a different app/screen or maybe this harness description is approximate. The editor search bar options are icon buttons, positioned to the right of the text field. Maybe in the intended build they should be above? Hmm.\n\nWait—maybe there's a \"search and replace dialog\" in the File Browser search? No replace. Maybe in view mode? Hmm.\n\nActually, Markor has \"Find & Replace\" in editor (the inline bar). The checkboxes (Match case, whole word, regex) appear as icon toggles to the right of inputs. The note might be describing a change that's not visible in this build's implementation because the harness uses Markor 2.x with a custom search bar. Hmm.\n\nCould be that the \"option checkboxes\" are in the file browser search dialog: Regex search, Case sensitive, Search in content — and that dialog has them below the input. Wait, the note says \"Search and replace dialog\" not \"file browser search\". Hmm.\n\nPerhaps there's a separate \"Replace\" dialog triggered by long-press? Let me explore editor's overflow after selecting text? We saw Cut/Copy/☰/Share; the ☰ might open more options (maybe \"Paste\", \"Select all\"?). Hmm.\n\nLet's search for a search/replace dialog in the app: maybe in the text editor's \"Search\" icon gives inline search; there's also \"Find in selection\". The \"option checkboxes\" might be the icon buttons; perhaps the bug is that they're laid out below/overlapping the fields? It looked fine.\n\nWait, maybe the seeded bug is about the *file browser's search dialog* (which has checkboxes) and the description accidentally says \"search and replace\". But the area list says \"editing actions and search/replace\" — likely editor.\n\nLet me test search/replace edge cases: empty search, replace with empty, regex, preserve case, replace all when no match. We can test on Regex.md/Regex2.md with regex 'cat@home' vs 'cat@home dog@home' — those preconditions strongly hint at regex search tests! Regex.md contains 'cat@home'; Regex2.md contains 'cat@home dog@home'. Why these? Likely to test:\n- Regex search: e.g., search `cat@home` with regex on → @ has no special meaning in the app's regex? Actually `@` literal. Hmm.\n- Or match whole word: searching \"cat@home\" should match exactly in Regex.md but in Regex2.md maybe substring?\n- Money.md 'Costs $5 and $10' hints at replace with `$` in replacement, e.g., regex `\\$(\\d+)` replacement `$$$1`? Testing regex replacement with $ group references.\n- Single.md one line 'gamma' with no newline at end — testing search/replace or save on no trailing newline.\n- Indent.md/Indent2.md hints for list indentation / regex anchors.\n\nSo the areas likely test search/replace with these data:\n- Regex.md 'cat@home' - test regex \"cat@home\" maybe @ considered special? No.\n- Regex2.md 'cat@home dog@home' - test match count (2 matches?).\n- Money.md 'Costs $5 and $10' - test replacement strings with $ (e.g., replace \"$5\" with \"€5\").\n- Single.md no newline - test appending at end / search match at end.\n\nThe \"option checkboxes\" might refer to checkboxes in a \"Search and replace dialog\" whose layout changed. Maybe the build has an actual dialog when you tap the editor's search icon on some devices? But we saw inline bar.\n\nHold on—maybe the file browser's action_search opens a dialog with checkboxes, and that's what's described. Let's look at that dialog layout again: it had Search edit at y=973, then checkboxes Regex/Case/Content below. The note says checkboxes now placed above search and replace input fields — that's the opposite of what we saw for file browser search (checkboxes below input, and no replace). Hmm.\n\nWhat if the editor's inline search UI in this build has the option icons in a row; but if you rotate the device, layout changes? Unlikely.\n\nMaybe the \"search and replace dialog\" is part of \"Search\" in the file browser when \"Search in content\" checked? No.\n\nLet me check the editor search options more: Long-press the \"match case\" etc.? No.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's a \"Search & Replace\" dialog in the view mode \"search\" (magnifier) button. Let's test: in view mode, tapping Search icon probably opens an in-page find. Could have a replace? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe I should look at file settings? No.\n\nLet's consider that the harness description might be intentionally misleading/general; we just need to test areas for bugs. Focus on behaviors and find seeded bugs. The changed list gives hints about where bugs were introduced. Four changes:\n1. View mode Markdown converter GFM tables (tested; seems working, but maybe bug in specific scenario).\n2. Search and replace dialog checkboxes above input fields (maybe a layout bug: checkboxes overlapping fields?).\n3. File browser quick-access marking kept up to date by its own handlers alone (bug could be: the favourite mark not updating when changed elsewhere, e.g., after renaming/deleting a favourited file, the Favourites list stale).\n4. Editor step back/forward controls: tracker attached once document has content (bug: undo/redo state wrong for empty documents or initial content).\n\nFor #3, \"marks kept up to date by its own handlers alone\" suggests there is a shared \"marks\" (favourite) cache used by file browser and maybe the quick-access dialog. Bug might be: when a file is deleted or changed, the favourite mark remains (stale), or favouriting in the Favourites view doesn't update main list. Let's test quick-access marking more:\n- Favourite a file in browser, go to Favourites, verify.\n- From Favourites, unfavourite, verify it disappears (done).\n- Delete a favourited file: the Favourites list should remove it. Let's test: favourite a file (e.g., Single.md), then delete it? That would destroy precondition data—bad. Instead rename a favourited file and check mark persists and list updates. Renaming is safe if we rename back. Or favourite a file and then check it appears/disappears correctly after rename.\n\nActually \"quick-access marking\" may refer to the \"QuickAccess\" marks in the bottom nav? Hmm, but Favourites is the likely one.\n\nAlso file browser's \"marks\" could be the icon shown for file types? No.\n\nLet's test favourite + rename + delete using QATable/QAEmpty (our test files, safe to delete). Plan:\n1. Favourite QATable.md.\n2. Go to Favourites → shows QATable.md.\n3. Rename QATable.md to QATable2.md in browser (from main list).\n4. Check Favourites now shows QATable2.md (and not old).\n5. Delete QATable2.md → check Favourites empty.\n\nBut wait, the file browser main list may keep mark icon (star). There's no visible star in list items (desc used only title+date). So marks are only visible in Favourites view. Good.\n\nLet's also test \"unfavourite from main list\" and verify Favourites empty (done earlier, somewhat).\n\nBefore that, deal with QAEmpty current state. I typed X and save is enabled. Let's press back to save. Then continue.\n\nAlso need to restore Indent.md? We restored \"child\" and saved. Its mtime changed but content original. Fine.\n\nThe test files QATable.md and QAEmpty.md will be deleted at the end; that's fine, they're ours.\n\nLet's go back to browser now."}
