{"type": "thinking", "text": "Favourites is EMPTY after renaming QATable.md → QATableR.md. Is that expected? A rename should ideally preserve the favourite mark, so Favourites should show QATableR.md. This looks like the seeded bug: \"File browser quick-access marking: the browser's marks are now kept up to date by its own handlers alone.\" The mark cache isn't updated on rename, so the renamed file loses its favourite. Or maybe the rename operation intentionally drops the mark (since the path changed, the favourite points to the old path). But UX expectation: Rename should keep the mark (the app usually updates marks on rename). Let me check whether re-adding and then renaming shows similar.\n\nActually wait—could the favourite have been lost because I favourited then renamed and the mark is keyed by old path; the Favourites folder lists only existing files with marks. Since the old path no longer exists, it shows nothing. That's the \"marks kept up to date by its own handlers alone\" bug: rename handler doesn't update the mark to the new path (previously a shared handler did). Yes, plausible seeded bug.\n\nBut is it definitely expected that rename preserves favourite? In Markor, \"Favourite\" marks stored as paths in shared prefs. When renaming, the app should update favourite paths. I'd expect yes.\n\nTest delete: favourite QATableR.md then delete it; Favourites should become empty (probably works since file missing). And test rename again to see if reproducible. Let's re-favourite QATableR and rename it back to QATable and check Favourites. Currently Favourites empty. Go back to Documents: tap \"..\" (element 5) → /storage; then Notebook. Or Go to (1) → storage root → Notebook. Let's tap Notebook via \"..\"? Actually tap element 5 \"..\" goes to /storage root list then tap Notebook."}
