{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now revisit the empty-doc undo bug. We need to be confident before filing. We saw QAEmpty (created empty, opened with empty content): typing \"test\" left Undo disabled; after hiding keyboard and waiting, still disabled. However, when I reopened QAEmpty (with content \"test\" at open), editing then Undo enabled. So the bug: undo/redo controls stay disabled for edits made in a document that was empty when opened, until the document is reopened. Actually careful: after typing \"test\" in the newly created empty file, then closing and reopening (content loaded \"test\"), the tracker attaches. So indeed \"tracker attached once the document has content\" at load time only; if content is empty at load, tracker isn't attached, and content added later doesn't attach it.\n\nBut the observed symptom is Undo/Redo disabled. Is that what the \"changed in build\" describes? \"Editor step back/forward controls: the change tracker is now attached once the document has content.\" Maybe intended: after loading, if content exists, attach tracker. Bug: if doc is empty at load, never attaches even after content typed. That's exactly what we saw. Solid.\n\nLet's reproduce one more time cleanly with a new file to confirm and file report. Use our existing QAEmpty.md — but currently it has content \"X\" and will open with content, so tracker would attach. To reproduce, we need a document empty at open. QAEmpty currently contains \"X\" (we changed from \"test\" to \"X\" earlier and saved). We can empty it by deleting content? If we open QAEmpty (non-empty) and select all delete, trackers attached at open so undo will work. That's not the condition.\n\nWe could create a new file again. Fine, create QAEmpty2.md and test. But we already reproduced twice (QATable and QAEmpty initial). The first time with QATable we observed disabled Undo/Save after typing table, and now I'm not 100% sure it was after keyboard hidden. But QAEmpty first session: typed \"test\" → undo/save disabled while keyboard open and after BACK+3s wait still disabled → then back and the file saved. That's a clean reproduction with wait.\n\nBut note: after BACK (hide keyboard) and wait, Save disabled. Then pressing BACK left the editor and the content did persist (autosave) — so Save disabled didn't prevent saving. So symptom is just controls disabled. Is that severe? It means Undo/Redo don't work in that session. It's the area under test (step back/forward controls) and clearly a functional bug.\n\nWait, one more consideration: maybe the toolbar appeared disabled in the accessibility tree because the editor had focus with keyboard previously and the app dims? No, visual screenshot earlier showed Undo/Save grayed? We haven't screenshotted the toolbar in that state. Let me verify with a fresh empty file and screenshot to make sure the disabled state is real and not just accessibility. We'll create a new test file QANew.md, type text, hide keyboard, screenshot, then tap Undo and see if it does anything.\n\nBut creating another file increases test data; we'll delete all our test files at the end. Fine.\n\nAlternative: we could use the existing QAEmpty and empty it by editing with undo? Hmm no.\n\nLet's create a new file \"QAUndo.md\": FAB → type → OK → type \"abc\" → hide keyboard → wait → screenshot → tap Undo. If undo does nothing (content stays \"abc\"), the bug is confirmed visually. Then go back, delete file.\n\nWait: we must be careful about what happens on tap Undo when disabled: nothing. Let's do it.\n\nTap FAB (41)."}
