{"type": "thinking", "text": "Tap had no effect: content still \"abc\", Undo still disabled. Bug confirmed: after typing into a freshly created (empty) document, Undo/Redo stay disabled and cannot undo.\n\nNow file report. Current screen is editor \"QAUndo\"; element_ref 1 (Undo button) from latest observe; observed_quote: the toolbar has no text; the element's desc is \"Undo\". The observed_quote needs exact text seen on screen showing the defect. The Undo button has description \"Undo\" but no visible text. We could quote the editor content \"abc\" to show document is non-empty while Undo disabled. observed_quote \"abc\". Hmm, that's on screen. The defect is the disabled Undo control; the quote can't show disabled state. But we can quote the content \"abc\" and explain. Alternatively, no quote (allowed for missing). But symptom_type \"no_effect\" maybe better: Undo has no effect. We'll use symptom_type \"no_effect\", expected: Undo enabled and reverts \"abc\" to empty; observed: Undo disabled, tapping it does nothing, content remains \"abc\".\n\nWhere: screen \"Editor (QAUndo.md) — toolbar\". Element \"Undo button (action_undo)\". element_ref 1. observed_quote \"abc\" (the editor text visible while Undo is disabled). Steps:\n1. Files > FAB > create new empty Markdown file QAUndo.\n2. Type \"abc\" in the editor.\n3. Close keyboard, wait; Undo/Redo remain disabled.\n4. Tap Undo: no effect, \"abc\" remains.\n\nBut wait—when the keyboard is open, Undo also disabled. Could it be a general transient? When document is opened with content, Undo becomes enabled right after text change. We verified with QAEmpty reopened: typing X → after keyboard hide Undo enabled. So specifically new/empty-at-open docs.\n\nHmm, but let me reconsider: maybe the reason is this document was created with the \"Empty file\" template, and Markor treats brand new file as \"new file\" and sets the undo tracker only after first save? The changed note says \"change tracker is now attached once the document has content\" — perhaps intended behavior is exactly that for new empty file, undo not available until content exists; but content now exists and it still isn't attached. So bug.\n\nReport it. Use observed_quote \"abc\". Let me also mention Save enabled (visual) but the core is Undo.\n\nActually, let me double check another scenario to strengthen: create new file and type with the on-screen keyboard vs type_text? The type_text uses adb input text which delivers key events; it should trigger text watcher. The undo tracker might rely on text watcher. It's fine.\n\nAlso test whether after pressing BACK (leave and immediately reopen, content non-empty) Undo works. It did for QAEmpty. So workaround reopen. Good.\n\nFile report."}
