are 4 changes: likely 4 bugs (or maybe fewer). Let's find the other two:\n\n#2 search and replace dialog checkboxes placement — maybe a functional bug where toggling the option checkboxes causes weird behavior, e.g., clicking a checkbox label toggles the wrong one, or checkbox states reset. We saw:\n- File browser search checkboxes persist (Search in content persisted).\n- Revealing \"Stop search after first match\" shifts layout, fine.\n- In editor, option icons toggle.\n\nPerhaps the bug is that \"Replace\" is placed in the same row as checkboxes? Hmm.\n\nLet's test the editor search more: place the option toggles and check behavior:\n- Match Case: search \"GAMMA\" in Single.md with case-sensitive should be 0; without should 1.\n- Whole word: search \"gam\" in Single.md whole-word should be 0, \"gamma\" 1.\n- Preserve Case: search \"gamma\" replace \"DELTA\" with preserve case → \"DELTA\"? Preserve case would map g→D? Hmm, preserve case applies when replacement case differs, e.g., \"Gamma\" -> \"Delta\". In Markor, Preserve Case option applies to replacements; if search is \"cat\" and replacement \"dog\", matches \"Cat\" → \"Dog\". Let's test on Regex.md 'cat@home'? Only lowercase. Not meaningful.\n\nCould test \"Find in Selection\": select part of text then search within selection. Complex.\n\nCould test \"Line based search\": search \"child\" in Indent.md with line-based on → shows the whole line maybe.\n\nCould test \"History\": after several searches, history shows previous terms. Let's test quickly: open Regex2, search, history button (element 8) shows list of past searches? Let's try on Money or any.\n\nActually, the changed note about search/replace might be a *layout* bug: In the replace row, the inputs and option icons may be misaligned such that the \"Replace\" field is above the option icons or checkboxes are above fields, with the replace field partially cut off. In our portrait layout, search field at y=378, replace at y=504, both visible. Fine. In landscape, if search bar stayed open, might be cut. But rotation closes search.\n\nHmm, wait. Rotation closed the search bar because Android recreated the activity. But is that expected? On rotation, Markor likely restores the fragment state, including search bar? If the seeded bug were about search bar layout, rotating would show it. But the closing might itself be the search-state loss bug. Let me test: open search, enter term \"cat\", rotate → search bar gone. Then rotate back → still gone. This loses search/replace inputs on rotation. Is that a \"bug\" a developer would accept? The hint says option checkboxes moved above fields—maybe in landscape the dialog is a \"dialog\" that gets recreated and the checkboxes position matters. Not convinced.\n\nLet me look for a different \"search and replace\" screen: maybe in *To-Do* or *QuickNote*? No.\n\nCould be in the \"More > Settings\" there's \"Search & Replace\" feature? Hmm.\n\nLet's check the file browser \"More options\" menu — maybe there's a \"Search & replace\" (recursive replace) feature! Let's tap More options (4) and see menu items."}
