{"type": "thinking", "text": "This is a plain SearchView, no replace, no checkboxes. Not our \"search & replace dialog\".\n\nOK, let me approach from a different angle: find all \"checkboxes\" in the app. The file browser search dialog has checkboxes. Perhaps the change note actually refers to this dialog and the expected ordering is checkboxes above the input (maybe the harness QA expects them above now). In our build they are below. But could there be a bug: When \"Search in content\" is checked, the dialog grows and the new \"Stop search after first match\" checkbox appears *below* the others; maybe on landscape or small screens the OK button is cut off. Let's rotate while this dialog is open to see. That's a plausible layout bug seed: \"option checkboxes are now placed above the search and replace input fields\" might have introduced a cut-off dialog in landscape? Hmm.\n\nLet's test rotation with the file-browser search dialog open (with content checked, 4 checkboxes). If OK button goes off-screen or dialog cut off, that's a bug. But rotation of a dialog likely recreates/dismisses.\n\nLet me not speculate. Instead, test the *editor* search/replace in landscape—we saw it closes on rotate. That could be the \"search and replace dialog\" state bug: rotation dismisses search/replace and loses entries. But changed note doesn't mention rotation.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the app has a *separate* \"Search and replace\" dialog in the editor's overflow that we haven't found. Let's check the floating toolbar \"☰\" menu; maybe it has \"Search & replace\" option. In selection toolbar, tap ☰ (element 23 in earlier). Let's return to editor and try. We are in view mode search now. Press BACK to close search (first back may close SearchView), then Edit Mode, select some text, tap ☰.\n\nActually, when text is selected, the floating toolbar has Cut, Copy, ☰, Share. The ☰ likely expands to more actions like \"Paste\", \"Select all\", \"Search\", \"Replace\"? Let's see. This might reveal a \"Find & Replace\" dialog. Let's test.\n\nCurrently in view-mode search with keyboard. Press BACK (hide keyboard), BACK (close search?), etc. Let's observe."}
