{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored. Good. Now leave the editor and make sure Indent.md saved original. Press BACK twice.\n\nThen maybe final: remove test files QAEmpty, QAUndo; restore Indent2.md name; clean favourites.\n\nBefore that, consider whether to report rotation closing search bar. Let's test explicitly on editor: open Indent.md editor, open search, type \"item\", toggle replace, type \"zzz\", rotate to landscape, observe. If the search UI vanishes and text lost—state loss. Is it worth a report? The task's \"Device: rotate the screen, and check that nothing is lost\" encourages reporting if content lost. The document content is preserved; only transient search query lost. Developers might treat as known/accepted. I'd rather not file unless it's clearly a bug. But it might be the seeded bug #2! \"Search and replace dialog: the option checkboxes are now placed above the search and replace input fields.\" Maybe the layout in landscape is broken? Hmm.\n\nLet's test the file browser search dialog rotation: if dialog closes on rotate, also state lost.\n\nActually, let's test a more targeted scenario for the search/replace layout: Open the editor search with replace, and inspect the positions of the search field and replace field and their option icons. The hint says checkboxes now above the fields. In our UI, they're to the right of each field, not above. Maybe that's the regression: options are expected above the inputs but instead are beside them? That's not a functional bug though; could be a layout mismatch to flag? The QA's job is bugs; visual layout inconsistency could be a bug if it causes overlap. Nothing overlaps.\n\nWait, maybe on a narrower width? The device is 1080 wide; the search bar fills. In landscape, if search bar were shown, fields might extend beyond. But it closes.\n\nMaybe I can force search bar to persist across rotation? Not possible.\n\nLet me try another route: open the editor search in landscape mode directly (rotate first, then open search). Then we can inspect layout in landscape. Good idea! Rotate to landscape while in editor, then open search, ensure all controls visible/unobstructed.\n\nLet's do that now: we're in Indent editor, keyboard maybe open. Press BACK to hide keyboard. Rotate landscape. Then tap Search.\n\nFirst press BACK (hide keyboard)."}
