{"type": "thinking", "text": "Search bar closed on rotation. So rotating closes the search/replace bar (and loses query/replace text). Is that a bug? It's a state loss, but maybe Android recreates activity and Markor doesn't persist search state. It could be pre-existing behavior, not a seeded regression. The \"changed\" list doesn't mention rotation. I'll note it but likely not report. Hmm, the instructions say \"Device: rotate the screen, and check that nothing is lost.\" If something is lost, we should report. The search query and replace text are lost, and the search UI is closed. Is that \"something\"? Yes, but is it a bug? It's arguably a bug/regression. But could be accepted behavior. Let's weigh: filing a report that gets rejected is okay? The instructions say a quote never on screen gets rejected. It doesn't say false reports penalized, but \"Signing off while bugs remain is worst\". Filing extra plausible bug is fine, but could also be considered incorrect. Hmm.\n\nLet me test whether the document text persists across rotation (it does) and whether other UI state like view mode persists (we saw view mode remained). Search bar is transient; many apps keep it. I lean towards not reporting unless it's tied to hint. The hint #2 is about search/replace dialog layout (checkboxes above inputs) — perhaps rotating could reveal a bug in the new layout. But we saw the bar closes before we can inspect... wait, maybe the closing is the bug! Because with the new layout maybe they didn't save state? No.\n\nHold on—maybe there's a *dialog* version of search/replace that appears when tapping \"Search\" in the file browser's selected-file context? Hmm.\n\nLet me try a different exploration: maybe the \"search and replace dialog\" is opened via the editor's *More options > Search* (if any). The editor More options had File Settings, Share, Tools, File Browser, Info, Reload. No search.\n\nAnother thought: the \"option checkboxes\" might refer to the *file browser search dialog* and the harness hint simply swapped terms. In that dialog, the checkboxes are below the search field in our build. Maybe the seeded bug is that when you check \"Search in content\", the additional checkbox \"Stop search after first match\" appears *below* and the dialog is repositioned so the search field/checkbox alignment gets messed? Not likely.\n\nLet's test the file browser search dialog *in landscape* to see if checkboxes/field overlap/cut off. Rotate landscape, open search, content checked. This tests layout. Let's do it (we're in editor; press BACK to browser, rotate, search).\n\nActually, first exit to browser. Press BACK (we're in editor; keyboard hidden; should go browser)."}
